### 22. `App.jsx` main fetch effect has a stale-closure risk with `connectSSE`
**File:** [App.jsx L60-93](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/src/App.jsx#L60-L93)

The `connectSSE` function at line 95 is defined outside the `useEffect` but uses `setProducts`, `setFacets`, and `setIsLoading` from the closure. When the effect cleanup runs (line 92), it sets `isCancelled = true` — but SSE callbacks (`evtSource.onmessage`) bypass `isCancelled` entirely. The `sseRef.current.close()` on line 63 does abort the connection, but **the `onerror` fallback** on line 154-164 will still fire and call `setProducts` with stale data.

