### 33. No `Content-Security-Policy` or security headers  
**File:** [index.js](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/server/index.js)

Despite `helmet` being in `package.json`, it's never used. The server has **no security headers** — no CSP, no X-Frame-Options, no HSTS. External scraper image URLs (`unsplash.com`, `rukminim.in`, etc.) are loaded directly in `<img>` tags, which CSP should whitelist.

---

### 34. Font files loaded from Google CDN with no fallback
**File:** [index.html L9-11](file:///c:/Users/Shikhar%20Mahajan/Documents/Project/Ekarters/index.html#L9-L11)

Fonts `Plus Jakarta Sans` and `Outfit` are loaded from `fonts.googleapis.com`. If the CDN is blocked (common in enterprise networks), the app will fall back to `system-ui`, but there'll be a visible FOUT (Flash of Unstyled Text) since `font-display: swap` is used.

